  "explanation": "A morbilliform rash is a measles-like maculopapular eruption and can be seen with several childhood infections, including roseola infantum, Epstein-Barr virus infection, Kawasaki disease, and scarlet fever. Influenza can also occasionally be associated with a morbilliform-type viral exanthem. Therefore, 'All of the above' is the best answer.",
